STYLE & VISUAL LANGUAGE

Hyper-detailed anime realism · crisp ink linework · dramatic contrast · large-scale environmental physics
Volumetric water sprays · micro-droplets · teal/azure ocean palette
Fast parallax movement · deep shadows · cinematic grading
No soft drifting shots — all camera moves are energized and motivated

AUDIO

Deep sub-bass rumble of the incoming wave
Wind shear · snapping wires · rattling signs
No music until final seconds → atmospheric tension
Impact roar sync’d with wave collapse

CAMERA

Mix of dolly, drone, handheld, underwater, and wide establishing shots
Rapid transitions, always motivated by motion
Lens palette: 35mm → 18mm → 50mm → 12mm → 70mm macro → 24mm wide
Zero static frames after anchor

ENVIRONMENT PHYSICS

Water behaves with realistic mass and velocity
Foam fragmentation, turbulent vortices, refractive caustics
Road dust lifting, signs flapping, cables whipping
Spray hitting lens with refraction distortions
Clouds boiling with rising convection

GOAL & TONE

Capture the overwhelming energy of the tsunami just before it hits —
cinematic dread, beauty, and unstoppable force.

SCENE BREAKDOWN

SCENE 0 - ANCHOR SHOT (0.0–0.3s)
Action:
• Micro-motions: waves churn, cloud edges billow, power lines tremble, sunlight flickers across the water.
• No character motion yet.
• Camera locked for 0.3 seconds, then a hard cut / whip transition.

SCENE 1 — THE PULLBACK (0.3–2.0s)

Camera: fast dolly backward down the coastal road.
Action:
• The massive wave towers higher with parallax.
• Sea spray blasts past frame edges.
• Shadows of clouds race across the town.
FX: strong wind noise, rattling wires, lens speckled with droplets.

SCENE 2 — SUBSURFACE SURGE (2.0–4.0s)

Camera: plunges beneath the water line into the belly of the tsunami.
Action:
• Rocks tumble violently underwater.
• Massive underwater currents swirl; teal light shafts cut through bubbles.
• Foam trails whip upward toward the surface.
Mood: deep, crushing power.

SCENE 3 — STREET-LEVEL RUSH (4.0–6.0s)

Camera: handheld at waist height, running down the narrow street.
Action:
• Power lines whip overhead.
• Shop banners flap violently.
• Water droplets and dust hit the lens.
FX: dynamic camera shake, fast footstep parallax, wind screams.

SCENE 4 — OVER-THE-ROOF SWEEP (6.0–8.0s)

Camera: drone-like glide over rooftops toward the central hill.
Action:
• The wave’s shadow engulfs the town.
• Cloud formations swirl as if pulled by the wave’s mass.
• Foamy tendrils begin curling at the crest.
VFX: long streaks of reflective sunlight across the water wall.

SCENE 5 — THE BREAK (8.0–11.0s)

Camera: dramatic tilt-up from street level to the collapsing crest.
Action:
• The wave begins folding forward, enormous.
• Water fractures into millions of micro-filaments.
• Rocks and debris suspended midair for a split second.
Sound: the low-end roar peaks.

SCENE 6 — WHITEOUT IMPACT (11.0–14.5s)

Camera: ultra-slow-motion close-up of the wave smashing downward.
Action:
• Explosion of water, foam, and refracted light.
• Impact spray forms abstract streaks and ink-like anime lines.
• Everything becomes a blinding white-blue blast.
FX: lens fully drenched, shimmering caustics, vibrating frame.

SCENE 7 — TITLE CARD (14.5–15.0s)

Black screen.
Faint water reflections shimmer across the text as if viewed through ripples:

TIDAL VEIL
Soft rumbling fades into silence.